  "scientific_conclusion": "Prospective four-channel NIRPS_V3_3 near-infrared (0.98-1.80 um YJH) SETI survey across 152 R=70,000 NIRPS_HE exposures of 22 nearby stars (27 control exposures on 4 verified zero-planet stars + 125 science exposures across 18 exoplanet hosts at 1.30-38.57 pc, including 5 full transit nights, 13 solar-neighborhood <10 pc stars, and the <2 pc ESPRESSO+NIRPS panchromatic bridge on Proxima Centauri and Barnard's Star) completed: across 1,971 synthetic trials, Channel K_PLANET Keplerian de-Doppler stacking boosted moving-planet CW recovery at >=6.5 sigma/exp from 3.7% to 58.0%, while NIRPS_V3_3 collapsed Legacy V2's 3828 near-IR false alarms to 0 control and 0 automated science candidates, setting 8-sigma 10 m laser limits down to 607.7 W (1064.1 nm down to 607.7 W; 1550.0 nm down to 1026.1 W) and completing an 80-unique-star (501-exposure, 0.38-1.80 um) Panchromatic V3 Survey."
